# TechJob Analytics — Project Constitution

## Architecture Principles

This project is a **multi-layer data intelligence platform** for the Moroccan IT job market. Raw listings are scraped from ReKrute and Emploi.ma, cleaned and normalized through a Python ETL pipeline into a star schema, served via a FastAPI REST backend, and visualized in both a React dashboard and Power BI. Every layer is independently replaceable. Prefer **simple, explicit data flow** over abstraction layers — the path from Parquet → API → chart should be traceable in under 30 seconds of reading. **Convention over configuration**; every file has a single, obvious home.

---

## 1. Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Frontend framework | React 19 with functional components + hooks |
| Build tool | Vite 6 |
| Language | TypeScript 5.8 (strict mode) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 — utility classes only |
| Routing | react-router-dom v7 |
| Data fetching | @tanstack/react-query v5 (with DevTools) |
| Charts | Recharts v3 |
| Icons | lucide-react (tree-shaken imports) |
| Animations | `motion` v12 |
| Backend API | FastAPI 0.115 (Python) |
| API server | Uvicorn 0.32 |
| Validation | Pydantic v2 |
| Data pipeline | Python (Pandas, NumPy) — Jupyter notebooks |
| Database engine | DuckDB in-memory OLAP over Parquet files |
| Data format | 13 Parquet files in star schema (10,782 job postings) |
| Reporting | Power BI (`.pbix` files consuming star schema CSVs) |

---

## 2. Conventions

### Folder Structure
```
techjob-analytics-react-router/
├── src/
│   ├── components/       # One file per React component
│   ├── modules/         # Feature modules (dashboard, etc.)
│   │   ├── components/  # Module-specific components
│   │   ├── hooks/       # Module-specific hooks
│   │   └── pages/       # Module-specific pages
│   ├── lib/             # Library configuration (API client, etc.)
│   ├── types/           # TypeScript interfaces
│   ├── App.tsx          # Root component (view router)
│   └── main.tsx         # Entry point
backend/
├── main.py              # FastAPI application entry
├── db.py                # DuckDB connection manager
├── schemas/             # Pydantic models
├── data/parquet/        # Parquet data files
└── requirements.txt     # Python dependencies
projet-data-maroc-tech/
├── notebooks/           # Jupyter ETL notebooks
└── data/                # Raw, clean, and star_schema CSV directories
```

### Naming
- **Components:** PascalCase, default export (`export default function TechJobDashboard`)
- **Hooks:** camelCase with `use` prefix, named export (`export function useGrowthData`)
- **Files:** camelCase for utilities and hooks (`useDashboardData.ts`), PascalCase for components (`TechJobDashboard.tsx`)
- **Types:** PascalCase interfaces in `src/types/`
- **API query keys:** camelCase strings matching the resource name (`'growthData'`, `'techRadar'`)

### Code Patterns
- All React Query hooks live in module-specific hook files (e.g., `modules/dashboard/hooks/useMarketData.ts`)
- Components import types from `src/types/` — never define shared types inside a component file
- Path alias `@/` maps to project root — use for cross-directory imports (`@/components/Foo`), relative imports for same-directory
- Filter state is managed via URL search params — no global state store

---

## 3. Constraints (What NOT to Do)

### Frontend
- **No inline styles** — all styling via Tailwind utility classes defined in the theme
- **No state management library** — React built-in state + TanStack Query is sufficient
- **No direct API URL construction outside `lib/api.ts`** — all endpoints are centralized there
- **No class components** — functional components + hooks only
- **No CSS modules, styled-components, or Emotion** — Tailwind v4 only
- **No custom CSS class names** — the `@theme` block in `index.css` defines the full design system

### Backend
- **SQL queries through DuckDB are allowed and expected** — DuckDB is the analytical engine
- **DuckDB uses an in-memory connection over Parquet data for zero-copy analytics**
- **No ORM is used in production backend code** — no SQLAlchemy, Prisma, Drizzle, or similar in runtime code
- **PostgreSQL/Supabase are not runtime dependencies** — they are migration/storage tooling only (see MIGRATION.md)
- **Do not introduce a relational database** unless explicitly directed

### Data Pipeline
- **No rewriting the star schema** — it is finalized (9 dims, 1 fact, 3 bridges); extend by adding rows to existing Parquet files, not by restructuring
- **No committing large Parquet files to git** — data files live on disk, `.gitignore` already excludes them

### General
- **No `any`** — use `unknown` with type narrowing, or define an explicit interface
- **No `// @ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error`** — fix the type properly
- **No hardcoded secrets** — environment variables are injected via `.env` at runtime
- **No npm packages outside `package.json`** — verify before importing anything new

---

## 4. AI Session Rules

### Before Implementing Anything
1. Read `spec.md` or `requirements.md` if present at project root
2. Read the relevant target file(s) in full before editing
3. Check `src/lib/api.ts` before writing a new API call
4. Check `src/types/` before defining new interfaces
5. Check existing components before creating a new component (compose or extend first)

### When Ambiguity Arises
STOP. Present exactly **2–3 options** with concrete trade-offs:
- Maintenance burden (will this break on the next dep upgrade?)
- Performance cost (is this adding latency or bundle size?)
- Consistency debt (does this deviate from the existing pattern?)

Do NOT proceed until the user selects one.

### After Implementing
1. Run `npm run lint` (tsc --noEmit) — fix all type errors
2. Run `npm run build` — verify the production bundle compiles
3. Verify backend starts if changes were made to `backend/`
4. Do NOT commit unless explicitly asked

---

*Updated to reflect actual runtime architecture: DuckDB + Parquet + SQL*
